RFC 7950 Section 7.17: "The target node MUST be either a container, list,
choice, case, input, output, or notification node."

Entry.Augment calls target.merge without checking target.Dir or target node
kind. When an augment (top-level, cross-module, chained, uses-expanded, or
uses-local) targets a leaf or leaf-list, Entry.merge panics with assignment to
entry in nil map (Entry.Dir is nil). When an augment targets an anydata,
anyxml, rpc, or action node, Entry.merge silently inserts child nodes that RFC
7950 Section 7.17 forbids.

Verify before target.merge that target.Dir is non-nil and target is one of the
seven permitted node kinds (container, list, choice, case, input, output, or
notification). Otherwise record an error on e naming the augment's source
location, target path, target node kind, and RFC 7950 Section 7.17, increment
processed so the augment retry loop does not spin, and skip target.merge.

No upstream pull request is opened yet. Remove this patch when the pinned
upstream release includes the correction. Apply after goyang-uses-augment.patch
in the canonical sorted patch set.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a vendored
module".

